messages:
hana: Quick report: sample Android SDK shows inconsistent retry behavior on 401 when using Retrofit + OkHttp on API 30. Some uploads are retried automatically and sometimes the app crashes with IllegalStateException: closed.

vic: can you paste the code path? are you using an Interceptor or Authenticator for token refresh?

hana: sample used an Interceptor to refresh token synchronously via a coroutine block. snippet: 
```kotlin
override fun intercept(chain: Interceptor.Chain): Response {
  var req = chain.request().newBuilder().header(\"Authorization\", \"Bearer ${tokenProvider.get()}\").build()
  val resp = chain.proceed(req)
  if (resp.code == 401) {
    runBlocking { tokenProvider.refresh() }
    req = req.newBuilder().header(\"Authorization\", \"Bearer ${tokenProvider.get()}\").build()
    return chain.proceed(req)
  }
  return resp
}
```

omar: that's risky. runBlocking inside an OkHttp interceptor can deadlock or re-enter network stack. Also if the request has a streaming RequestBody it's not replayable and calling chain.proceed twice can fail.

vic: recommended: switch to OkHttp Authenticator for 401 refresh so it runs on OkHttp's internal thread pool and will get a fresh call. Also protect streaming bodies: either buffer small payloads or mark endpoints non-retriable.

hana: we updated sample to Authenticator and added a tiny helper that wraps RequestBody into a ReplayableRequestBody when small (<1MB) otherwise it disables retry. That fixed most flakes.

omar: add unit test with MockWebServer that returns 401 then accepts second request and ensure no IllegalStateException. Also test with a paused server that resumes mid-upload to simulate slow networks.

ci-bot: flaky job: sample-app-instrumented (api30) failed 2/6 runs, failing test: UploadRetryTest.testNoRetryOnStreamingBody.

hana: added test fix: use temp file fallback for large body in test and ensure cleanup in finally block. Also added telemetry tag `retry_attempted=true/false`.

vic: one more thing: log pollution on older Androids when enabling OkHttp logging interceptor can OOM because it buffers bodies; ensure logging only enabled in debug.

hana: PR opened with sample changes and tests. tagging @pat for CI matrix run. thanks everyone.
